  "unplaced": [],
  "notes": "Lockheed Martin Grand Prairie: the only site figure that could be read on an open page is the city's 2020 one (4,000); the city's own pages and newer press figures (about 4,800 to 5,000) were not reachable from the research environment. Bell: \"Textron\" is deliberately not listed as an alias of Bell (Textron has other subsidiaries); existing \"Textron\" rows in the Dallas-Fort Worth area and Amarillo are very likely Bell sites and should be reviewed by hand. Bell's Grand Prairie Drive Systems Center (about 1,200 people in the city's 2020 report) and its Alliance plant now being fitted out at 15100 N Beach St, Fort Worth, are listed under unplaced. General Motors: GM says it employs over 9,000 in Texas, but that includes GM Financial and the Austin technical centre, so no state manufacturing figure is given. Tarrant County's list shows 10,512 for the Arlington plant, which does not match GM's own 5,400 and was not used. Tesla: the Megapack factory near Brookshire and the lithium refinery near Robstown are outside these two industries and are left to other briefs. SpaceX: McGregor is a test site rather than a factory but is kept because it is one of the company's three large Texas sites; the Bastrop Starlink plant is filed under Computer and Electronic Product Manufacturing."
}
